{
  "README": [
    "Declared coverage contract.",
    "",
    "This file is HAND-AUTHORED and says which",
    "(machine x system x card x geometry x depth x addressing) cells the",
    "integration suite is REQUIRED to cover, and which directory owes each",
    "one. It is never generated from a test run: a contract derived from what",
    "happened would be satisfied by whatever happened, and the one question it",
    "exists to answer — did a later change silently narrow coverage? — would",
    "become unanswerable.",
    "",
    "The achieved side is the @@COV records suite rows emit at runtime, read",
    "from the live machine. Diff the two with:",
    "",
    "    make -C tests/integration test TIER=matrix 2>&1 | tee run.log",
    "    python3 scripts/test-matrix.py --check run.log",
    "",
    "Check semantics:",
    "  declared and covered ......  ok",
    "",
    "Cells owed by a test in a DIFFERENT tier than the one being checked are",
    "reported separately, not as regressions — pass --tier=<unit|matrix|extended>",
    "so a PR-tier run is not blamed for extended-tier cells. The owing tier is",
    "read from the directory's own config.mk, so it cannot drift.",
    "",
    "  declared, NOT covered .....  FAILS (coverage regressed)",
    "  covered, not declared .....  warning: claim it so it becomes protected",
    "",
    "A `blocked` reason is stated in full on the cell, with the GitHub issue",
    "that tracks the defect where there is one. A defect that has code to",
    "reproduce it also has a row: a milestone row (row_end_milestone in",
    "lib/mac.script; it runs nightly, reports red and does not fail the",
    "suite) or a suite row that is skipped until the fix lands. A cell",
    "blocked by a media fact or an observability limit needs no row.",
    "",
    "Four declared-but-uncovered cases are warnings rather than failures,",
    "because none of them means coverage regressed:",
    "  suite:<dir> does not exist   the owing suite is not built yet. Derived",
    "                              from the filesystem, so it cannot be faked.",
    "  blocked: <reason>           the cell is unreachable today, for the",
    "                              reason given (a defect, a media fact or",
    "                              an observability limit).",
    "  media_gated: true           the row skipped because private test data is",
    "                              absent from this checkout.",
    "  owed by another tier        the owning directory's TEST_TIER differs",
    "                              from --tier=, so this run never had a",
    "                              chance to cover it. Read from that",
    "                              directory's config.mk, so it cannot drift.",
    "",
    "STILL NOT DECLARED, and deliberately so. Nothing below is waiting on",
    "work in progress; it is coverage that exists and passes but is not",
    "claimed:",
    "  * extended-tier app and diagnostic rows (mactest x4, marathon x2,",
    "    sysinfo x2, the installers). These assert an application's behaviour",
    "    rather than a (machine x system x card x geometry x depth) cell, so a",
    "    matrix row would restate the directory's own goldens without adding a",
    "    protected axis.",
    "  * the 6.0.8 rationalization's IIcx and IIfx floppy/HD split.",
    "The card-family display cells that used to sit here are now DECLARED:",
    "iicx-video-modes' 8 remaining JMFB cells, iicx-gsvrom's 12 generic-vROM",
    "cells, and suite-iix's 8 re-hosted sweep cells. They emit @@COV like any",
    "other row, so the contract now catches it if they stop covering what they",
    "cover. ROM-stage cells are labelled as such in their feature string, the",
    "shape iix-portrait-603 established.",
    "Under-declaration is stated here on purpose: it is visible in review",
    "rather than silently missing from the diff."
  ],
